## Per-item rounding (CONVENTIONS section 4, rule 2; quirk Q-R1)

Two W-2s of $30,000.40 and $20,000.40. DF rounds each box first, so line 1a is
$30,000 + $20,000 = $50,000. The 1040 instructions (add the cents, round the
total) would give $50,000.80, which is $50,001. The module follows DF.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestPerItemRounding:
  a scope MkW2
  b scope MkW2
  f scope W.FormW2s

scope TestPerItemRounding:
  definition a.writable_wages equals $30,000.40
  definition b.writable_wages equals $20,000.40
  definition a.writable_federal_withholding equals $3,000.49
  definition b.writable_federal_withholding equals $2,000.49
  definition a.writable_oasdi_withholding equals $1,860.40
  definition b.writable_oasdi_withholding equals $1,240.40
  definition a.writable_medicare_withholding equals $435.40
  definition b.writable_medicare_withholding equals $290.40
  definition f.w2s equals [a.w2; b.w2]
  definition f.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition f.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.NoCombatPay
  assertion f.wages = $50,000
  # The sum of the raw amounts rounds to $50,001; DF does not do that.
  assertion not (f.wages = $50,001)
  assertion f.form_w2_withholding = $5,000
  # 1860 + 1240 + 435 + 290 = 3825 (each box rounded first; the raw sum is
  # 3826.40, which would round to 3826)
  assertion f.social_security_taxes_withheld = $3,825
  assertion not f.unsupported
```

A tie rounds away from zero, as in Java `HALF_UP`.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestWagesTie:
  a scope MkW2
  b scope MkW2
  f scope W.FormW2s

scope TestWagesTie:
  definition a.writable_wages equals $10,000.50
  definition b.writable_wages equals $0.49
  definition f.w2s equals [a.w2; b.w2]
  definition f.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition f.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.NoCombatPay
  assertion f.wages = $10,001
```

## MFJ split by filer

Primary filer: two W-2s of $40,000 and $5,000.40 with $1,000 and $2,500 of
dependent care benefits. Spouse: one W-2 of $30,000.70. Line 1a is the sum of
all three; the per-filer wages (earned income for CDCC) are kept apart.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestMfjSplit:
  p1 scope MkW2
  p2 scope MkW2
  s1 scope MkW2
  f scope W.FormW2s

scope TestMfjSplit:
  definition p1.writable_wages equals $40,000
  definition p2.writable_wages equals $5,000.40
  definition p1.writable_dependent_care_benefits equals $1,000
  definition p2.writable_dependent_care_benefits equals $2,500
  definition s1.filer equals Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler
  definition s1.writable_wages equals $30,000.70
  definition f.w2s equals [p1.w2; p2.w2; s1.w2]
  definition f.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition f.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.NoCombatPay
  assertion f.primary_filer_wages = $45,000
  assertion f.secondary_filer_wages = $30,001
  assertion f.wages = $75,001
  assertion f.primary_filer_has_w2_wages_greater_than_0
  assertion f.secondary_filer_has_w2_wages_greater_than_0
  assertion f.primary_filer_dependent_care_benefits = $3,500
  assertion f.secondary_filer_dependent_care_benefits = $0
  assertion f.primary_filer_w2s_count = 2
  assertion f.secondary_filer_w2s_count = 1
  assertion not f.unsupported
```

A spouse W-2 on a return that is not MFJ still counts in line 1a (DF sums all
`/formW2s`), but not toward the MFJ-only combat pay of the spouse.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestSecondaryW2NotMfj:
  p scope MkW2
  s scope MkW2
  f scope W.FormW2s

scope TestSecondaryW2NotMfj:
  definition p.writable_wages equals $10,000
  definition s.filer equals Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler
  definition s.writable_wages equals $20,000
  definition s.writable_combat_pay equals $700
  definition f.w2s equals [p.w2; s.w2]
  definition f.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingSeparately
  definition f.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.NoCombatPay
  assertion f.wages = $30,000
  assertion f.mfj_spouse_combat_pay = $0
  assertion f.all_combat_pay = $700
  assertion not f.some_filer_has_combat_pay
```

## Form 8880 line 2: deferrals, 457(b) governmental or not

Box 12: D $4,000.40, E $1,000, G $2,000.60, H $300, S $150, AA $500, BB $250,
EE $125. Governmental 457(b): all of them count, G rounded to $2,001 first.
Not governmental: G is left out.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestDeferrals:
  gov scope MkW2
  non_gov scope MkW2
  f scope W.FormW2s
  g scope W.FormW2s

scope TestDeferrals:
  definition gov.writable_wages equals $50,000
  definition gov.deferrals_401k equals $4,000.40
  definition gov.deferrals_403b equals $1,000
  definition gov.deferrals_457b equals $2,000.60
  definition gov.deferrals_501c18 equals $300
  definition gov.simple_contributions equals $150
  definition gov.roth401k_contributions equals $500
  definition gov.roth403b_contributions equals $250
  definition gov.roth457b_contributions equals $125
  definition gov.plan_457b_is_governmental equals true
  definition non_gov.writable_wages equals $50,000
  definition non_gov.deferrals_401k equals $4,000.40
  definition non_gov.deferrals_403b equals $1,000
  definition non_gov.deferrals_457b equals $2,000.60
  definition non_gov.deferrals_501c18 equals $300
  definition non_gov.simple_contributions equals $150
  definition non_gov.roth401k_contributions equals $500
  definition non_gov.roth403b_contributions equals $250
  definition non_gov.roth457b_contributions equals $125
  definition non_gov.plan_457b_is_governmental equals false
  definition f.w2s equals [gov.w2]
  definition g.w2s equals [non_gov.w2]
  definition f.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition g.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition f.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition g.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition g.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.NoCombatPay
  definition g.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.NoCombatPay
  # 4000 + 1000 + 2001 + 300 + 150 + 500 + 250 + 125
  assertion f.primary_filer_total_deferrals_and_contributions = $8,326
  # same without the 2001 of code G
  assertion g.primary_filer_total_deferrals_and_contributions = $6,325
  assertion not (g.primary_filer_total_deferrals_and_contributions = $8,326)
  assertion f.secondary_filer_total_deferrals_and_contributions = $0
  # codes D, E, G, H, S, AA, BB, EE never knock out
  assertion not f.unsupported
  assertion not g.unsupported
```

## Combat pay (box 12 code Q)

MFJ, primary $5,000.40 and spouse $3,000. `/allCombatPay` is the rounded sum
of every W-2; `/combatPayAmount` (line 1i) follows the election.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestCombatPay:
  p scope MkW2
  s scope MkW2
  none scope W.FormW2s
  prim scope W.FormW2s
  both scope W.FormW2s
  spouse_not_primary scope W.FormW2s

scope TestCombatPay:
  definition p.writable_combat_pay equals $5,000.40
  definition s.filer equals Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler
  definition s.writable_combat_pay equals $3,000
  definition none.w2s equals [p.w2; s.w2]
  definition prim.w2s equals [p.w2; s.w2]
  definition both.w2s equals [p.w2; s.w2]
  definition spouse_not_primary.w2s equals [p.w2; s.w2]
  definition none.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition prim.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition both.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition spouse_not_primary.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition none.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition prim.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition both.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition spouse_not_primary.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition none.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition prim.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition both.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition spouse_not_primary.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition none.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.NoCombatPay
  definition prim.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.UsePrimaryNotSpouseCombatPay
  definition both.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.UseBothCombatPay
  definition spouse_not_primary.combat_pay_election equals
    W.CombatPayElection.UseSpouseNotPrimaryCombatPay
  assertion none.primary_filer_combat_pay = $5,000
  assertion none.mfj_spouse_combat_pay = $3,000
  assertion none.both_filers_has_combat_pay
  assertion not none.only_one_filer_has_combat_pay
  assertion none.all_combat_pay = $8,000
  assertion none.combat_pay_amount = $0
  assertion prim.combat_pay_amount = $5,000
  assertion both.combat_pay_amount = $8,000
  assertion spouse_not_primary.combat_pay_amount = $3,000
```

`UsePrimaryCombatPay` is only an option when the primary filer alone has combat
pay; offered when both have it, DF's `Switch` falls through to `$0`.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestCombatPayOptionMismatch:
  p scope MkW2
  s scope MkW2
  f scope W.FormW2s

scope TestCombatPayOptionMismatch:
  definition p.writable_combat_pay equals $5,000
  definition s.filer equals Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler
  definition s.writable_combat_pay equals $3,000
  definition f.w2s equals [p.w2; s.w2]
  definition f.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition f.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.UsePrimaryCombatPay
  assertion f.combat_pay_amount = $0
```

## HSA, box 12 code W

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestHsaContributions:
  p scope MkW2
  s scope MkW2
  mfj scope W.FormW2s
  single scope W.FormW2s

scope TestHsaContributions:
  definition p.employer_hsa_contributions equals $1,200.40
  definition s.filer equals Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler
  definition s.employer_hsa_contributions equals $800
  definition mfj.w2s equals [p.w2; s.w2]
  definition single.w2s equals [p.w2; s.w2]
  definition mfj.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition single.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition mfj.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition single.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition mfj.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition single.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition mfj.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.NoCombatPay
  definition single.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.NoCombatPay
  assertion mfj.primary_filer_total_hsa_contributions_from_w2s = $1,200
  assertion mfj.secondary_filer_total_hsa_contributions_from_w2s = $800
  assertion mfj.has_primary_filer_hsa_contributions_from_w2s
  assertion mfj.has_secondary_filer_hsa_contributions_from_w2s
  assertion mfj.total_hsa_contributions_on_w2s = $2,000
  assertion single.total_hsa_contributions_on_w2s = $1,200
  assertion single.has_hsa_contributions_on_w2
```

## Knockouts

Each case is a single W-2 that must send the return out of scope, and its
twin just inside the line that must not.

Box 8 allocated tips; box 11 nonqualified plans; box 13 flags.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestW2Knockouts:
  tips scope MkW2
  tips_rounds_to_zero scope MkW2
  nonqual scope MkW2
  statutory scope MkW2
  sick scope MkW2
  f_tips scope W.FormW2s
  f_tips0 scope W.FormW2s
  f_nonqual scope W.FormW2s
  f_statutory scope W.FormW2s
  f_sick scope W.FormW2s

scope TestW2Knockouts:
  definition tips.writable_allocated_tips equals $100
  definition tips_rounds_to_zero.writable_allocated_tips equals $0.49
  definition nonqual.writable_non_qualified_plans equals $1,000
  definition statutory.statutory_employee equals true
  definition sick.third_party_sick_pay equals true
  definition f_tips.w2s equals [tips.w2]
  definition f_tips0.w2s equals [tips_rounds_to_zero.w2]
  definition f_nonqual.w2s equals [nonqual.w2]
  definition f_statutory.w2s equals [statutory.w2]
  definition f_sick.w2s equals [sick.w2]
  definition f_tips.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition f_tips0.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition f_nonqual.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition f_statutory.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition f_sick.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition f_tips.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f_tips0.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f_nonqual.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f_statutory.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f_sick.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f_tips.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f_tips0.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f_nonqual.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f_statutory.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f_sick.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f_tips.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.NoCombatPay
  definition f_tips0.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.NoCombatPay
  definition f_nonqual.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.NoCombatPay
  definition f_statutory.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.NoCombatPay
  definition f_sick.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.NoCombatPay
  assertion f_tips.ko_flow_knockout_allocated_tips
  assertion f_tips.unsupported
  # $0.49 rounds to $0 before the test, so it is not a knockout
  assertion not f_tips0.ko_flow_knockout_allocated_tips
  assertion not f_tips0.unsupported
  assertion f_nonqual.ko_flow_knockout_non_qualified_plans
  assertion f_nonqual.unsupported
  assertion f_statutory.ko_flow_knockout_statutory_employee
  assertion f_statutory.unsupported
  assertion f_sick.ko_flow_knockout_third_party_sick_pay
  assertion f_sick.unsupported
```

Box 12 knockout codes. The test uses the unrounded amount: `$0.40` in code A
knocks out although it rounds to `$0`. Code W (HSA) on a W-2 of a filer who can
be claimed as a dependent is a knockout; without the dependency it is not.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestBox12Knockouts:
  code_a scope MkW2
  code_k scope MkW2
  code_ii scope MkW2
  code_c scope MkW2
  code_q scope MkW2
  code_w scope MkW2
  f_a scope W.FormW2s
  f_k scope W.FormW2s
  f_ii scope W.FormW2s
  f_c scope W.FormW2s
  f_q scope W.FormW2s
  f_w_dependent scope W.FormW2s
  f_w_independent scope W.FormW2s

scope TestBox12Knockouts:
  definition code_a.uncollected_oasdi_tax_on_tips equals $0.40
  definition code_k.golden_parachute_excise_tax equals $50
  definition code_ii.non_taxable_medicaid_waiver_payments equals $1
  definition code_c.taxable_life_insurance_over_50k equals $12.34
  definition code_q.writable_combat_pay equals $500
  definition code_w.employer_hsa_contributions equals $1,000
  definition f_a.w2s equals [code_a.w2]
  definition f_k.w2s equals [code_k.w2]
  definition f_ii.w2s equals [code_ii.w2]
  definition f_c.w2s equals [code_c.w2]
  definition f_q.w2s equals [code_q.w2]
  definition f_w_dependent.w2s equals [code_w.w2]
  definition f_w_independent.w2s equals [code_w.w2]
  definition f_a.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition f_k.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition f_ii.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition f_c.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition f_q.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition f_w_dependent.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition f_w_independent.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition f_a.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f_k.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f_ii.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f_c.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f_q.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f_w_dependent.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals true
  definition f_w_independent.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f_a.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f_k.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f_ii.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f_c.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f_q.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f_w_dependent.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f_w_independent.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f_a.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.NoCombatPay
  definition f_k.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.NoCombatPay
  definition f_ii.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.NoCombatPay
  definition f_c.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.NoCombatPay
  definition f_q.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.NoCombatPay
  definition f_w_dependent.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.NoCombatPay
  definition f_w_independent.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.NoCombatPay
  assertion f_a.ko_knockout_for_box12_value
  assertion f_a.unsupported
  assertion f_k.ko_knockout_for_box12_value
  assertion f_ii.ko_knockout_for_box12_value
  assertion not f_c.ko_knockout_for_box12_value
  assertion not f_c.unsupported
  assertion not f_q.ko_knockout_for_box12_value
  assertion not f_q.unsupported
  assertion not f_w_independent.ko_knockout_for_box12_value
  assertion not f_w_independent.ko_knockout_for_box12_dependency
  assertion not f_w_independent.unsupported
  assertion f_w_dependent.ko_knockout_for_box12_dependency
  assertion not f_w_dependent.ko_knockout_for_box12_value
  assertion f_w_dependent.unsupported
```

## Medicare wages and Form 8959

Thresholds `P.additional_medicare_tax_threshold_*`: $200,000 single, $250,000
joint, $125,000 separate. The test is "greater than", so exactly the
threshold is fine. In a joint return one spouse over $200,000 knocks out
even if the total is under $250,000.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestMedicareWages:
  p_at scope MkW2
  p_over scope MkW2
  p_joint scope MkW2
  s_joint scope MkW2
  p_split scope MkW2
  s_split scope MkW2
  p_mfs_over scope MkW2
  single_at scope W.FormW2s
  single_over scope W.FormW2s
  mfs_over scope W.FormW2s
  mfs_at scope W.FormW2s
  joint_at scope W.FormW2s
  joint_over scope W.FormW2s
  split_over_individual scope W.FormW2s

scope TestMedicareWages:
  definition p_at.writable_medicare_wages equals $200,000
  definition p_over.writable_medicare_wages equals $200,001
  definition p_joint.writable_medicare_wages equals $125,000
  definition p_mfs_over.writable_medicare_wages equals $125,001
  definition s_joint.filer equals Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler
  definition s_joint.writable_medicare_wages equals $125,000
  definition p_split.writable_medicare_wages equals $200,001
  definition s_split.filer equals Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler
  definition s_split.writable_medicare_wages equals $10,000
  definition single_at.w2s equals [p_at.w2]
  definition single_over.w2s equals [p_over.w2]
  definition mfs_over.w2s equals [p_mfs_over.w2]
  definition mfs_at.w2s equals [p_joint.w2]
  definition joint_at.w2s equals [p_joint.w2; s_joint.w2]
  definition joint_over.w2s equals [p_over.w2; s_joint.w2]
  definition split_over_individual.w2s equals [p_split.w2; s_split.w2]
  definition single_at.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition single_over.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.HeadOfHousehold
  definition mfs_over.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingSeparately
  definition mfs_at.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingSeparately
  definition joint_at.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition joint_over.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition split_over_individual.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition single_at.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition single_over.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition mfs_over.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition mfs_at.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition joint_at.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition joint_over.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition split_over_individual.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition single_at.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition single_over.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition mfs_over.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition mfs_at.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition joint_at.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition joint_over.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition split_over_individual.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition single_at.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.NoCombatPay
  definition single_over.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.NoCombatPay
  definition mfs_over.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.NoCombatPay
  definition mfs_at.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.NoCombatPay
  definition joint_at.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.NoCombatPay
  definition joint_over.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.NoCombatPay
  definition split_over_individual.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.NoCombatPay
  assertion single_at.medicare_wages_additional_tax_threshold = P.additional_medicare_tax_threshold_other
  assertion single_at.form_w2_total_medicare_wages = $200,000
  assertion not single_at.ko_knockout_medicare_wages
  assertion not single_at.unsupported
  assertion single_over.ko_knockout_medicare_wages
  assertion single_over.any_filer_required_to_pay_extra_medicare_tax
  assertion single_over.unsupported
  # MFS: $125,000 of wages is exactly the $125,000 threshold, $125,001 is over
  assertion mfs_at.medicare_wages_additional_tax_threshold = $125,000
  assertion not mfs_at.ko_knockout_medicare_wages
  assertion mfs_over.ko_knockout_medicare_wages
  # MFJ: $250,000 total is exactly the threshold, each spouse under $200,000
  assertion joint_at.medicare_wages_additional_tax_threshold = $250,000
  assertion not joint_at.ko_knockout_medicare_wages
  assertion not joint_at.any_filer_exceeds_eligible_for_medicare_wages_credit
  assertion not joint_at.unsupported
  # MFJ: $325,001 total
  assertion joint_over.ko_knockout_medicare_wages
  assertion joint_over.any_filer_exceeds_eligible_for_medicare_wages_credit
  assertion not joint_over.any_filer_required_to_pay_extra_medicare_tax
  # MFJ: total $210,001 is under $250,000 but the primary filer has $200,001
  assertion split_over_individual.form_w2_total_medicare_wages = $210,001
  assertion split_over_individual.any_filer_exceeds_eligible_for_medicare_wages_credit
  assertion split_over_individual.ko_knockout_medicare_wages
  assertion split_over_individual.unsupported
  assertion split_over_individual.max_medicare_wages_for_any_filer_on_return = $200,001
```

## Social security wage base across employers

Wage base `P.oasdi_wage_base` is $168,600. Two W-2s of the same filer with
$100,000 and $68,600 of social security wages total exactly the base (no
knockout); $68,601 is over. A single W-2 over the base is not a knockout
because the test needs two W-2s. A W-2 above the base is capped at the base
per W-2. Wages of the two spouses do not add.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestOasdiWageBase:
  a scope MkW2
  b_at scope MkW2
  b_over scope MkW2
  single_big scope MkW2
  spouse scope MkW2
  at_base scope W.FormW2s
  over_base scope W.FormW2s
  one_w2 scope W.FormW2s
  spouses_apart scope W.FormW2s

scope TestOasdiWageBase:
  definition a.writable_oasdi_wages equals $100,000
  definition b_at.writable_oasdi_wages equals $68,600
  definition b_over.writable_oasdi_wages equals $68,601
  definition single_big.writable_oasdi_wages equals $200,000
  definition spouse.filer equals Types.FilerRole.SecondaryFiler
  definition spouse.writable_oasdi_wages equals $100,000
  definition at_base.w2s equals [a.w2; b_at.w2]
  definition over_base.w2s equals [a.w2; b_over.w2]
  definition one_w2.w2s equals [single_big.w2]
  definition spouses_apart.w2s equals [a.w2; spouse.w2]
  definition at_base.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition over_base.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition one_w2.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition spouses_apart.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition at_base.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition over_base.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition one_w2.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition spouses_apart.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition at_base.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition over_base.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition one_w2.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition spouses_apart.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition at_base.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.NoCombatPay
  definition over_base.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.NoCombatPay
  definition one_w2.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.NoCombatPay
  definition spouses_apart.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.NoCombatPay
  assertion at_base.primary_filer_total_oasdi_wages_for_knockout = $168,600
  assertion not at_base.ko_any_filer_exceeds_max_oasdi_wages
  assertion over_base.primary_filer_total_oasdi_wages_for_knockout = $168,601
  assertion over_base.primary_filer_exceeds_max_oasdi_wages
  assertion over_base.ko_any_filer_exceeds_max_oasdi_wages
  assertion over_base.unsupported
  # one W-2 capped at the base: count is 1, so no knockout
  assertion one_w2.primary_filer_total_oasdi_wages_for_knockout = $168,600
  assertion not one_w2.ko_any_filer_exceeds_max_oasdi_wages
  # each spouse has one W-2: no knockout either
  assertion not spouses_apart.ko_any_filer_exceeds_max_oasdi_wages
  assertion spouses_apart.primary_filer_w2s_count = 1
  assertion spouses_apart.secondary_filer_w2s_count = 1
```

## Satisfiable inputs and rejected bad outputs

A return with ordinary W-2 data has no knockout, and the module's output for it
is not an arbitrary one: a wrong line 1a, 25a or Schedule 8812 figure is
rejected.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestOrdinaryReturn:
  a scope MkW2
  f scope W.FormW2s

scope TestOrdinaryReturn:
  definition a.writable_wages equals $52,000
  definition a.writable_federal_withholding equals $4,100
  definition a.writable_oasdi_wages equals $52,000
  definition a.writable_oasdi_withholding equals $3,224
  definition a.writable_medicare_wages equals $52,000
  definition a.writable_medicare_withholding equals $754
  definition f.w2s equals [a.w2]
  definition f.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.Single
  definition f.primary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f.secondary_filer_can_be_claimed equals false
  definition f.combat_pay_election equals W.CombatPayElection.NoCombatPay
  assertion f.wages = $52,000
  assertion f.form_w2_withholding = $4,100
  assertion f.social_security_taxes_withheld = $3,978
  assertion not f.unsupported
  # known-bad outputs are not what the module computes
  assertion not (f.wages = $51,999)
  assertion not (f.form_w2_withholding = $0)
  assertion not (f.social_security_taxes_withheld = $3,224)
```
